# Woodright public-launch CORS - EXAMPLE ONLY, not loaded by any running process.
#
# Copy relevant lines into the real production env when the buyer-facing
# cutover is explicitly approved. Setting these alone does nothing: backend
# `apps/backend/medusa-config.ts` only *validates* against the production
# buyer shape when `WOODRIGHT_LAUNCH_CORS_PROFILE=production_buyer` is also
# set (see ops/config/public-launch/launch-env.production-candidate.example
# for the private-candidate bake, which intentionally does NOT set this
# profile yet).

# Buyer-facing storefront origins - must be exactly these two once public.
STORE_CORS=https://woodright.ru,https://www.woodright.ru

# Admin stays private - loopback/VPN-restricted only, never a public
# admin.woodright.ru host. Fill with the real private/VPN admin origin(s)
# used by the operator, not a public host.
ADMIN_CORS=http://127.0.0.1:9000,http://127.0.0.1:5173

# Auth endpoints are shared by storefront + admin origins that need to call
# /auth - keep this list as narrow as STORE_CORS + ADMIN_CORS combined.
AUTH_CORS=https://woodright.ru,https://www.woodright.ru,http://127.0.0.1:9000,http://127.0.0.1:5173

# Opt-in gate that makes apps/backend/medusa-config.ts validate the two vars
# above with assertProductionStoreCors / assertProductionAdminCors
# (apps/backend/src/lib/launch-cors.ts). Leave unset until the buyer-facing
# cutover is explicitly approved - see that file's top comment for why this
# is opt-in rather than automatic.
# WOODRIGHT_LAUNCH_CORS_PROFILE=production_buyer

# If running as a private production_candidate (never public) and QA also
# needs to reach the API from a loopback storefront preview, the validator
# allows exactly one extra origin next to the two production origins above:
# STORE_CORS=https://woodright.ru,https://www.woodright.ru,http://127.0.0.1:3200
# (requires WOODRIGHT_RUNTIME_EXPOSURE=private and
#  WOODRIGHT_RUNTIME_ROLE=production_candidate at the same time)
